WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.070
In 1637, the philosopher René Descartes
compared animals to machines, without

2
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.220
minds.

3
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:12.770
Centuries earlier, Genesis had given
humans dominion over every living thing.

4
00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.950
Today, people still
farm animals, eat them,

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.910
and hunt them for sport.

6
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.350
So is it wrong to farm,
eat or hunt animals,

7
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.230
or does that depend on what animals are?

8
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.410
In this mission, you'll climb a
ladder of views on who counts morally,

9
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.640
from machines to rights.

10
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.440
Then you'll weigh up whether
animals should have rights,

11
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.720
or whether welfare is enough.

12
00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:39.360
Your mission: work out how
each view judges farming,

13
00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.330
eating and hunting animals.
